{"id":"granicus-1-449","platform":"granicus","body":"City Council","name":"Equestrian Committee Meeting","date":"2020-06-22","time":"","canceled":false,"agenda_url":"https://rollinghillsestatesca.granicus.com/AgendaViewer.php?view_id=1&clip_id=449","minutes_url":"https://rollinghillsestatesca.granicus.com/MinutesViewer.php?view_id=1&clip_id=449&doc_id=b9bdacd3-0330-11eb-80dd-0050569183fa","packet_url":"","clip_id":449,"view_id":1,"video_url":"https://rollinghillsestatesca.granicus.com/MediaPlayer.php?view_id=1&clip_id=449","transcript_url":"","mp4_url":"","mp3_url":"","agenda_text":"CITY OF\n\n  ROLLING HILLS ESTATES\n  4045 PALOS VERDES DRIVE NORTH • ROLLING HILLS ESTATES, CA 90274\n  TELEPHONE 310.377.1577 • FAX 310.377.4468\n  www.RollingHillsEstatesCa.gov\n\n  Regular Meeting Agenda\n  EQUESTRIAN COMMITTEE\n\nMonday, June 22, 2020  7:00 PM  Teleconference\n\nPursuant to the Governor's Executive Order N-29-20, Equestrian Committee Members will be participating via\nteleconference.\n\n- Committee meeting videos are live-streamed on the City’s website at www.rhe.city and available for viewing.\n\n- Members of the public may listen to the meeting live by calling: (1-669-900-6833) from any phone, Meeting ID:\n896 9813 5303, Meeting Password: 361369. (Please note you will not have the ability to speak using the call-in\noption from a phone line.)\n\n- Public correspondence may be emailed to the Cynthia Morquecho, Community Services Supervisor at\ncynthiam@rollinghillsestatesca.gov. Emails received before 5:00 p.m. the night of the meeting will be forwarded\nto the Committee for their consideration and included as part of the record.\n\n- Members of the public may comment online using eComment on the “Meeting Agendas, Minutes & Videos”\npage of the City’s website (www.rhe.city/MeetingAgendas). Once the agenda is published, there will be an\n“eComment” button next to the linked agenda under \"Upcoming Events\". Follow this link to the City’s SpeakUp\npage. After you register, you may comment on any item on that particular agenda. These comments can be seen\nby the public, will be considered by the Committee and become part of the record.\n\n- Members of the public who wish to speak during this meeting may join the Zoom meeting by accessing the\nZoom app from a computer (downloaded at Zoom.com) or tablet or phone (downloaded in the App Store), by\nentering the following credentials: Meeting ID: 896 9813 5303, Meeting Password: 361369\n\nMembers of the public who join the Zoom meeting will not have video, and may request to speak using the\nfollowing process: After joining the Zoom meeting, if you wish to speak, please select the \"raise hand\" option at\nthe lower portion of your screen. The City Clerk will send you a chat message to identify which item on the\nagenda you would like to speak on and will unmute your mic at the appropriate time.\n\nAgenda reports and other disclosable public records relating to each agenda item are available on the City's\nwebsite under Meeting Agendas, Minutes & Videos at www.rhe.city\n\nEQUESTRIAN COMMITTEE  Page 1\n6/22/2020\nAmericans With Disabilities Act: In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act, if you require a disability-related\nmodification or accommodation to attend or participate in this meeting, including auxiliary aids or services, please call the\nCity Clerk's office at (310) 377-1577 at least 48 hours prior to the meeting.\n\fEquestrian Committee  Regular Meeting Agenda  June 22, 2020\n\n1.  CALL TO ORDER\n\n2.  ROLL CALL\n\n3.  APPROVAL OF MINUTES\n\n  A.  EQUESTRIAN COMMITTEE MEETING MINUTES OF MAY 11, 2020\n\n  Attachments: Draft Minutes\n\n4.  AUDIENCE ITEMS WRITTEN /ORAL COMMUNICATIONS NOT ON AGENDA\n\n5.  DISCUSSION ITEMS\n\n  A.  CALIFORNIA  WATER  SERVICE  COMPANY  WATER  RELIABILITY\n  PROJECT (VERBAL REPORT)\n\n6.  STAFF ITEMS\n\n  A.  TERMINATION OF CITY OF ROLLING HILLS ESTATES EASEMENT FOR\n  BRIDLE TRAIL PURPOSES ON TRACT NO. 27980, IN THE CITY OF\n  RANCHO PALOS VERDES\n  Attachments: Staff Report\n\n  B.  COVID-19 UPDATE (VERBAL REPORT)\n\n  C.  SPECIAL EVENTS UPDATE (VERBAL REPORT)\n\n  D.  REQUEST FOR PLAYGROUND STRUCTURE AT CHANDLER PARK\n\n  Attachments: Staff Report\n\n  E.  STATUS OF HORSE SHOWS (VERBAL REPORT)\n\n  F.  EQUESTRIAN ISSUES LOG\n\n  Attachments: Equestrian Issues Log\n\n  G.  WASTE MANAGEMENT MANURE RATE INCREASE\n\n  Attachments: Staff Report\n\n7.  COMMITTEE REPORTS\n\nEQUESTRIAN COMMITTEE  Page 2\n6/22/2020\nAmericans With Disabilities Act: In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act, if you require a disability-related\nmodification or accommodation to attend or participate in this meeting, including auxiliary aids or services, please call the\nCity Clerk's office at (310) 377-1577 at least 48 hours prior to the meeting.\n\fEquestrian Committee  Regular Meeting Agenda  June 22, 2020\n\n  A.  ADOPT-A-TRAIL (VERBAL REPORT)\n\n8.  FUTURE AGENDA ITEMS\n\n9.  ADJOURNMENT\n  The next Equestrian Committee meeting will be held on Monday, July 27, 2020 at 7:00 p.m.\n\nEQUESTRIAN COMMITTEE  Page 3\n6/22/2020\nAmericans With Disabilities Act: In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act, if you require a disability-related\nmodification or accommodation to attend or participate in this meeting, including auxiliary aids or services, please call the\nCity Clerk's office at (310) 377-1577 at least 48 hours prior to the meeting.","minutes_text":"PK\u0003\u0004\u0014\u0000\u0006\u0000\b\u0000\u0000\u0000!\u0000\u000e,\\\u0011�\u0001\u0000\u0000:\b\u0000\u0000\u0013\u0000\b\u0002[Content_Types].xml �\u0004\u0002(�\u0000\u0002\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0